From 35e8ea44adbaa1c17d5dae1df6b9d4a9770ad662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sayed Kaif <skaif@digiscrypt.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:31:05 +0530
Subject: cap_flag: reject negative bit in the cap_iab_t vector accessors

cap_iab_get_vector() and cap_iab_set_vector() bound the requested
capability index with a single test, "bit >= cap_max_bits()".
cap_value_t is a signed int, so this signed comparison does not reject
a negative bit: for example -1 >= cap_max_bits() is false. The
functions then compute

    unsigned o = (bit >> 5);

and use o to index the fixed-size iab->i[], iab->a[] and iab->nb[]
arrays. For a negative bit the arithmetic right shift preserves the
sign, so the value converted to the unsigned index is enormous
(-1 >> 5 == -1, which becomes 0xFFFFFFFF). cap_iab_get_vector() then
reads, and cap_iab_set_vector() reads and writes, far outside the
heap-allocated iab object.

The sibling accessors cap_get_flag() and cap_set_flag() already reject
out-of-range indices with an explicit "value >= 0" test; the IAB
vector accessors only checked the upper bound. Add the matching
"bit < 0" check to both so a negative index is rejected the same way an
oversized one is (get returns 0, set returns -1/EINVAL) instead of
touching memory out of bounds.

Verified by compiling the real cap_flag.c and calling
cap_iab_set_vector(iab, CAP_IAB_INH, -32, CAP_SET): before the change
AddressSanitizer reports an out-of-bounds access at cap_flag.c:261
(index 0xFFFFFFFF); after the change the call returns -1/EINVAL, while
valid bits (e.g. 5) still succeed and the upper bound is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Sayed Kaif <skaif@digiscrypt.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew G. Morgan <morgan@kernel.org>
---
 libcap/cap_flag.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libcap/cap_flag.c b/libcap/cap_flag.c
index 94afd1e..7ce5909 100644
--- a/libcap/cap_flag.c
+++ b/libcap/cap_flag.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ int cap_fill(cap_t cap_d, cap_flag_t to, cap_flag_t from)
 cap_flag_value_t cap_iab_get_vector(cap_iab_t iab, cap_iab_vector_t vec,
 				    cap_value_t bit)
 {
-    if (!good_cap_iab_t(iab) || bit >= cap_max_bits()) {
+    if (!good_cap_iab_t(iab) || bit < 0 || bit >= cap_max_bits()) {
 	return 0;
     }
 
@@ -246,7 +246,7 @@ cap_flag_value_t cap_iab_get_vector(cap_iab_t iab, cap_iab_vector_t vec,
 int cap_iab_set_vector(cap_iab_t iab, cap_iab_vector_t vec, cap_value_t bit,
 		       cap_flag_value_t raised)
 {
-    if (!good_cap_iab_t(iab) || (raised >> 1) || bit >= cap_max_bits()) {
+    if (!good_cap_iab_t(iab) || (raised >> 1) || bit < 0 || bit >= cap_max_bits()) {
 	errno = EINVAL;
 	return -1;
     }
